From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 08:45:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bind each system's last-played game and the console's last
 game
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A system view can show a system's counts but not the game played there
last, nor the game played last on the whole console. A home that offers
to continue a system's game needs both.

- {system:lastPlayed}: the game with the newest lastplayed among the
  system's displayed games; {system:continue}: that game, else the
  best-rated favorite (else the best-rated game), for systems never
  played. Every game property follows: {system:lastPlayed:name},
  ...:image, ...:developer. Computed with the other counts and kept as
  paths, resolved on use, so a removed game is never dereferenced.
- {system:hasLastPlayed} and {system:hasContinue} are true only while
  the game still resolves. hasContinue is false on tools, emulators and
  the screenshot viewer (hardware type tool, emulator or system, or a
  group of those): what they ran last is shown, but not offered to run
  again. A collection's last game and pick leave those systems out.
- {game:lastplayedTime} ("HH:MM") and {game:lastplayedDays} (calendar
  days since: 0 today, 1 yesterday, -1 never), so a theme can write
  "Today · 18:17", "Yesterday" or a date in its own language; the
  lastplayed date binding has no time.
- {global:lastPlayed}: the game played last on the console, tools and
  screenshots left out. es-core has no system list, so BindingManager
  gets registerGlobalProperty() and the app registers it after loading
  the systems.

A game's own system kept its counts until its game list reloaded:
refreshCollectionSystems (game played, favorite toggled, metadata
saved) now resets the counts of the game's system and its group too.
The system view also binds its extras again when shown, so coming back
from a game shows the new counts and last game.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
